{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final CI-runtime investigation stocktake. Objective remains an average Gerrit Verify wall clock of 20-30 minutes with unchanged fidelity/behavioral/contract coverage and lower runner occupancy.\n\nLanded improvements during the session: coverage now runs only on Ubuntu 3.13; the complexity lock moved from four matrix cells to one job (206 runner-seconds removed); bridge schedule parsing was hoisted from all 1,440 minutes; AST provenance is indexed once (cold scan 3.26s to 0.81s); redundant Pandoc subprocess renders were replaced with static expected outputs while the complete real-Pandoc corpus replay moved to External Integration; repeated fixture repositories became isolated templates (103.416 measured worker-seconds removed); the reverse-DNS editor fixture 35.013s long pole was eliminated; docs-only routing retains generated-doc, drift, reference-validation, and other documentation gates while skipping code suites; an organic non-doc change verified the full suite still runs; superseded same-change runs cancel promptly.\n\nLatest clean five-run series before the final experiment: mean end-to-end 31m28.8s, median 31m20s, macOS job mean 27m56.2s, mean time through macOS completion 30m13.4s, and final-vote queue mean 65.8s. Therefore the target is not yet proven. No normal macOS test exceeded 20s in the captured organic control; the remaining N=3000 import benchmark ranged around 19.69s hosted and 20.19-21.63s locally, with 13.69s attributed to its 24 contractually required Git add/commit pairs.\n\nFinal experiment: APFS RAM-disk placement had strong maintained-OSS precedent (Apple Git CI, Aeron, Git performance guidance) but failed the predeclared rebar retention oracle. Exact no-RAM control 31868300174: default 17m26s, macOS job 20m36s. Treatments: 18m43.77s, 20m54.61s, 18m26s, and final run 31873067707 at 20m00.60s default. Every treatment was 5.5-20% slower; recursive reporting/release added 71-98s. The experiment was fully reverted in Gerrit 1806, merged as 7d908fbbc6da12f8e274b3ef1e3a2357377799ef. Final run 31873067707 was green, macOS 24m42s, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments. It also replicated the repaired owner-nonwritable snapshot cleanup and nested-pytest cache hygiene on the trusted-main workflow. Ticket unplayful-inaccurate-muskrat received signed plan PASS plus completion PASS and was closed.\n\nOpen disposition: inedible-subsimious-brahmancow remains the parent occupancy/runtime goal. panpsychic-clever-hawk records 4/4 direction-level OSS consensus for eliminating per-test Git subprocesses, projected around 75s macOS wall / 207 runner-seconds, but no fidelity-preserving implementation reached consensus; do not auto-implement. ravenous-beribboned-walleye retains the exact N=3000/6,000-event/24-commit contract and needs a disposition based on hosted evidence versus the local long pole. Several organic full runs after the no-RAM revert are required before claiming the 20-30 minute average. Per operator direction, pause here and take stock rather than start another remediation or control run."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786783829695184001,"uuid":"4b103c80-7bdb-4a16-9418-ddbe5452001b"}